**Member Variable:** you can define the member variables inside Entity or Util class to store values. Values stored in the variable/s are shared across Actions of a particular Entity Instance but should be defined carefully( if really needed) as this has the memory implications. Instance of the Entity class is available throughout the Transaction, the complete rule chain for an Entity is executed on the same instance.

- Member variables are defined inside class and outside actions.

- Static member/local variables must not be used. The static variables are shared across all users and all Transactions. Get approval from Project lead before use.

- Variables defined inside an action are only accessible locally.

- Variables should be defined carefully( if really needed) as this has the memory implications.

Naming Convention:

- Variable names can contain alphabets and numeric digits.

- Can not contain spaces and special characters, except the underscore (_).

- Variable names cannot begin with a digit.

