| A transaction is a sequence of operations performed (using one or more Query statements) on a database as a single logical unit of work. The effects of all the Query statements in a transaction can be either all committed (applied to the database) or all rolled back (undone from the database).
In a Controller, Model is defined and has a name. Transaction can share the same name or could be different. In case if you need an additional transaction to perform some task in between the main transaction, create the transaction with parameter myTransactionName.
oController.getTransaction(myTransactionName);
To understand the Transaction concept, let’s see there is a scenario of “create delivery from an order”. In this case there are below three operations to be performed: • Create delivery
 Reserve the stock
 Update order All these operations should be either success or fail but together. Commit the transaction if all success or roll back if any one of them failed.
Commit Transaction.
Clear Transaction |
